1530
00:03:12,970 --> 00:03:17,470
I won't lay a hand on you.
I saw how you kick, I'd be too terrified to try.

1531
00:03:19,380 --> 00:03:21,530
I just want to have a little talk.

1532
00:03:30,760 --> 00:03:33,190
I'm from Maldura.

1533
00:03:34,730 --> 00:03:42,570
If I do kill you, I wonder if Sauslind
will remove its humane mask and go to war.

1534
00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:47,080
Just joking.

1535
00:03:48,710 --> 00:03:50,260
Here's a handkerchief.

1536
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:53,070
Oh, thank you.

1537
00:03:54,130 --> 00:03:57,060
We'll separate at the other exit and go back to the ball.

1538
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:04,510
Are you really from Maldura?

1539
00:04:04,510 --> 00:04:05,730
Half of me is.

1540
00:04:05,730 --> 00:04:06,730
Half?

1541
00:04:07,430 --> 00:04:14,730
My mother is from Sauslind. You can imagine
the environment I grew up in, right?

1542
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:18,740
Was it a political marriage?

1543
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:23,490
No. It's said they met by chance and fell in love.

1544
00:04:23,950 --> 00:04:28,840
As long as the blood of either country runs through me,
I feel the burden of both their histories.

1545
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:33,460
In the past, it's true that Maldura
has waged war against Sauslind many times,

1546
00:04:34,010 --> 00:04:38,040
and I'm aware that Sauslind
sees Maldura as an uncivilized country.

1547
00:04:39,250 --> 00:04:46,140
That's why I was so surprised
when I heard of your proposal of support for my country.

1548
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:52,690
I offer my thanks to you, Lady Elianna.

1549
00:04:52,690 --> 00:04:57,150
Due to your kindness,
we've avoided war with my mother's native country.

1550
00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:04,780
The Count called you an idealistic dreamer,
but I think that's fine.

1551
00:05:05,890 --> 00:05:11,090
Where does a country go if it's not following
the ideals of the person standing at the top?

1552
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:14,770
Lord Irvin...

1553
00:05:15,870 --> 00:05:22,340
If it's wrong is another matter.
The people around you aren't saying that it is.

1554
00:05:22,990 --> 00:05:28,350
That's why your plan will be introduced,
and the people of Sauslind will back you.

1555
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:32,850
So have some more pride.
You're the fiancÃ©e of the crown prince, right?

1556
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:36,230
Thank you!

1557
00:05:38,180 --> 00:05:42,820
By the way, it's time to stop being
so standoffish and come out.

1558
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:43,570
Huh?

1559
00:05:47,950 --> 00:05:49,140
Jean?

1560
00:05:50,950 --> 00:05:54,080
This guy is the true identity of the ghost of the old castle.

1561
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:55,250
Huh?

1562
00:05:55,250 --> 00:05:56,840
He's my attendant and as you can see,

1563
00:05:57,150 --> 00:06:02,340
he stands out, so I told him to conceal himself
and he was made into a ghost.

1564
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:16,610
My Lady, why does it seem like you enjoy
getting locked away in places like this?

1565
00:06:22,990 --> 00:06:24,530
Get the girl!

1566
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:26,730
Rei! Where's my sword?!

1567
00:06:26,730 --> 00:06:30,040
I don't know. Please do what you can without it.

1568
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:33,660
What a compassionate attendant you are.

1569
00:06:37,130 --> 00:06:37,960
Run away!

1570
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:41,460
This is where you indulge yourself and run.

1571
00:06:49,230 --> 00:06:50,430
Annâ€”

1572
00:06:50,690 --> 00:06:53,310
Tch, why the hell are there two women here?

1573
00:06:54,910 --> 00:06:57,190
Which one of you is Elianna Bernstein?!

1574
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:02,030
Which one?!

1575
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:15,370
Why would you do such a thing as step on a book?

1576
00:07:15,370 --> 00:07:18,040
I see you all are enemies of humanity.

1577
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:19,230
What...

1578
00:07:20,260 --> 00:07:26,510
I am Elianna Bernstein! Who are all of you?!
Tell me why you're here!

1579
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:31,010
What, we're just here to cause a small incident. Â

1580
00:07:31,010 --> 00:07:37,400
The fiancÃ©e of the crown prince of Sauslind and the prince
of Maldura will be murdered on their secret rendezvous.

1581
00:07:38,430 --> 00:07:40,400
The prince of Maldura?

1582
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:43,630
Which country is the criminal really from?

1583
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:46,900
Tensions will run through the gates of both countries again.

1584
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:52,910
You're creating a reason to invade this country.
That's why you're here, right?

1585
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:55,850
The Maldurans trying to forcefully spark a war

1586
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:58,370
are simply acting like a group of brainless thugs.

1587
00:07:58,370 --> 00:08:01,040
It's embarrassing as a fellow countryman.

1588
00:08:01,790 --> 00:08:07,800
Hearing words about being a "fellow countryman"
from a descendent of an enemy country is laughable!

1589
00:08:11,230 --> 00:08:12,720
You imbecile.

1590
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:20,650
If you keep thinking like that, Maldura will continue
being treated as a country of dim-witted barbarians.

1591
00:08:20,650 --> 00:08:21,730
What was that?!

1592
00:08:22,030 --> 00:08:24,730
You must be the underlings of the third prince, yeah?

1593
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:27,860
Shut up! Kill him!

1594
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:46,010
I leave for a just a little while
and all sorts of insects crawl out of the woodwork, eh?

1595
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:53,220
I'm home, Eli.

1596
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:58,730
Your Highness, why are you here?

1597
00:08:58,730 --> 00:09:02,980
How could I not show up when you're in danger, Eli?

1598
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:09,360
Besides, a little bird told me
that we had an unofficial foreign guest here.

1599
00:09:10,170 --> 00:09:16,410
Good grief. It would've gotten complicated had
I informed you, so I had to wait for the right time.

1600
00:09:16,410 --> 00:09:18,540
I don't understand, Uncle.

1601
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:24,040
His mother passed away last year,
so he came to visit Eidel in her stead.Â

1602
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:27,920
The young ladyâ€™s name was Sylvia Slade.

1603
00:09:29,260 --> 00:09:31,930
She was far too old to be called a "young lady" anymore.

1604
00:09:33,620 --> 00:09:39,000
Your Highness, for now, let's move elsewhere. 
Everyone will take notice of this commotion.

1605
00:09:41,530 --> 00:09:43,730
Some thieves got in?

1606
00:09:43,730 --> 00:09:45,940
The Prince has returned as well, apparently.

1607
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:50,570
Eli! My sister!

1608
00:09:52,520 --> 00:09:57,200
Are those ears just for decoration?!
I told you to be careful, didn't I?!

1609
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:59,660
Lilia, that hurts.

1610
00:09:59,660 --> 00:10:01,080
Lady Lilia.

1611
00:10:01,620 --> 00:10:06,340
Eli was lured out by someone
and got locked up in this castle.

1612
00:10:08,050 --> 00:10:12,140
I wonder who it was that spread around
that she was in the old castle?

1613
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:16,600
I-I, well...

1614
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:22,850
All right, listen up! That young lady
had nothing to do with the burglars!

1615
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:25,350
Rona?!

1616
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:32,040
I heard there was suspicion
that Lady Elianna's horse was tampered with,

1617
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:35,000
I assumed that the whoever had connections
with the burglars would be sneaking in,

1618
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:36,780
and I looked into the matter.

1619
00:10:36,780 --> 00:10:41,750
Then, I found this maid
who was using the young lady as a cover.

1620
00:10:42,700 --> 00:10:48,250
After Lady Elianna was locked away, we found her
relaying the news to the thugs and apprehended her.

1621
00:10:48,900 --> 00:10:52,880
The young lady was taken advantage of
due to the maid's instigation.

1622
00:10:53,780 --> 00:10:56,890
Taken advantage of... that can't be...

1623
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:03,560
I can't believe Lady Sophia...

1624
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:06,400
The duke won't get away with this either!

1625
00:11:06,830 --> 00:11:11,610
Lilia. Watch over Lady Sophia.

1626
00:11:11,610 --> 00:11:14,780
Jeez! You are way too nice to people, Eli!

1627
00:11:19,410 --> 00:11:21,750
C'mon, pull yourself together.

1628
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:25,350
Eli.

1629
00:11:26,270 --> 00:11:28,630
I agree with Lady Lilia.

1630
00:11:28,630 --> 00:11:31,170
Have more of an awareness of danger.

1631
00:11:32,050 --> 00:11:36,430
We can't have rumors of you with any other man but me.

1632
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:39,840
Okay.

1633
00:11:41,970 --> 00:11:44,060
I am thankful you are safe,

1634
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:46,940
Lady Elianna, Lady Anna.

1635
00:11:49,150 --> 00:11:55,660
Excuse me, Lady Kreis,
but were you acquainted with Lady Sylvia Slade?

1636
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:58,200
Yes...

1637
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,320
I pushed too hard.

1638
00:12:00,930 --> 00:12:02,530
Will you explain it then?

1639
00:12:04,180 --> 00:12:09,960
My mother was the only daughter of Duke Slade,
who ruled over the Eidel Domain.

1640
00:12:11,370 --> 00:12:14,590
My mother loved this land that she was born and raised on.

1641
00:12:14,590 --> 00:12:19,840
However, her father, Duke Slade,
attempted an insurrection against the royal family,

1642
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:22,820
and it was discovered that they were colluding with Maldura.

1643
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:30,440
At the time, my father... the present king of Maldura,
held the position of prince in those days,

1644
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:34,610
and he met my mother while investigating Sauslind.

1645
00:12:36,020 --> 00:12:41,490
I heard that at the time,
he was opposed to those who had plotted invasions.

1646
00:12:43,790 --> 00:12:52,420
My mother said she had no regrets in life.
I think all she wanted was to go back to the land she was born.

1647
00:12:53,310 --> 00:12:57,880
So I turned to Lady Kreis, who was a friend of my mother.

1648
00:12:57,880 --> 00:13:00,970
I'm sorry I got you involved in my situation.

1649
00:13:04,090 --> 00:13:06,470
Ladybird Sylvia.

1650
00:13:06,960 --> 00:13:09,480
It all makes sense now.

1651
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,660
Lord Theodore,

1652
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:18,240
you said Duke Slade's rebellion was brought to light
because there was secret intel from the inside.

1653
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:19,450
Yes.

1654
00:13:19,450 --> 00:13:22,990
Was that information from Lady Sylvia?

1655
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:30,750
It was. However, she was at the same time
branded as the daughter of a criminal,

1656
00:13:31,950 --> 00:13:33,990
so the facts were withheld.

1657
00:13:36,510 --> 00:13:41,760
Lord Irvin. Had Lady Sylvia
always loved this embroidery?

1658
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:44,600
You mean the little insects on it?

1659
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:50,860
I'd heard about it and thought it was strange,
but I thought it was my own mind playing tricks on me.

1660
00:13:54,090 --> 00:13:57,520
This insect's name is the "ladybird", or ladybug.

1661
00:13:58,880 --> 00:14:05,850
When it's springtime in the Eidel Domain, the entire area
is blanketed by the blooms of Eidel's white flower.

1662
00:14:06,890 --> 00:14:17,460
The ladybugs land only that flower. Due to that, they say
that the flowers of Eidel will not pollinate without the ladybugs,

1663
00:14:17,460 --> 00:14:23,050
therefore ladybugs are known by another name:
the Flower Protectors.

1664
00:14:23,760 --> 00:14:29,560
I will protect the land I was born and raised in.
It will not become a battleground.

1665
00:14:29,560 --> 00:14:33,060
I will be like those ladybirds that protect Eidel's flowers.

1666
00:14:42,340 --> 00:14:43,950
Count Hayden.

1667
00:14:45,060 --> 00:14:51,110
Though you might call it naive,
I still cannot choose to answer violence with violence.

1668
00:14:52,830 --> 00:14:57,710
Do you expect the one after your life
to say the same thing at times like this?

1669
00:14:58,740 --> 00:15:03,720
I will nip war in the bud
no matter how many times it grows back,

1670
00:15:04,290 --> 00:15:08,180
until people cease holding such ill ambitions in their hearts.

1671
00:15:09,670 --> 00:15:10,760
By doing so,

1672
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:16,190
when there is exchange between neighboring
countries without starting a war with Maldura,

1673
00:15:16,190 --> 00:15:20,690
the need for the Edea territories
to fear war should cease to exist.

1674
00:15:22,010 --> 00:15:25,240
You're proposing friendship with Maldura?

1675
00:15:32,090 --> 00:15:35,000
Just be yourself, Eli.

1676
00:15:38,200 --> 00:15:40,540
I understand that it will be difficult.

1677
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:46,010
No matter how steep or long that road is

1678
00:15:46,010 --> 00:15:49,930
we will never reach it if we donâ€™t take the first step.

1679
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:57,140
Lady Sylvia protected Eidel, protected her country,
without depending on the military.

1680
00:15:57,140 --> 00:16:04,900
Nobles tend to rely on force, but that's no different
than a bratty child who brags about his strength.

1681
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:11,530
I'd like you to follow the example of a woman
like Lady Sylvia on occasion.

1682
00:16:19,710 --> 00:16:22,790
The thoughts of an idealistic dreamer...

1683
00:16:23,750 --> 00:16:24,800
However,

1684
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:31,050
there is youth and potential in your words.

1685
00:16:32,100 --> 00:16:36,560
Lady Elianna Bernstein. As long as you are here,

1686
00:16:36,980 --> 00:16:41,310
I can have faith that our country
will not become a battleground.

1687
00:16:41,310 --> 00:16:49,810
I, Lowe Hayden, swear my loyalty to you
and the crown prince who chose you.

1688
00:16:53,770 --> 00:16:55,330
Count Hayden...

1689
00:16:55,880 --> 00:17:00,080
Your loyalty is as good as good as a blessing from the gods.

1690
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:04,590
I also swear to walk a path
that will not shame your loyalty.

1691
00:17:09,140 --> 00:17:12,340
Then I will also lay all my cards on the table. Â

1692
00:17:12,950 --> 00:17:18,390
This time, the number one reason I made a private visit
because I wanted to see my mother's home,

1693
00:17:18,390 --> 00:17:21,140
but I was also doing a preliminary examination.

1694
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:22,480
A preliminary examination?

1695
00:17:23,040 --> 00:17:24,920
The second prince of Maldura said

1696
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:30,360
he wanted me to determine whether or not
there was anyone we could foster good relations with here.

1697
00:17:32,180 --> 00:17:37,620
After meeting Lady Elianna, I felt I was also able
to get an inkling of Your Highness's character as well.

1698
00:17:37,880 --> 00:17:43,960
Will these attempts of friendship get us involved
in political infighting over Maldura's crown?

1699
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:49,630
At the very least, the supporters of the second prince,
including myself, do not want to go to war.

1700
00:17:50,100 --> 00:17:56,640
Even if you were not a supporter of that second prince,
there are many other options available.

1701
00:17:56,640 --> 00:17:58,810
You want me to make my case in more detail?

1702
00:17:58,810 --> 00:18:02,640
The rumors are true; you're more intelligent than you look.

1703
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:05,650
I will take that as a compliment.

1704
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:16,410
Well, Eli, there's nothing more to worry about,
so you can breathe easy today.

1705
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:23,170
Um, Your Highness...

1706
00:18:25,060 --> 00:18:29,170
I missed you very much... Your Highness.

1707
00:18:30,750 --> 00:18:31,670
Eli...

1708
00:18:33,860 --> 00:18:39,680
Elianna, I thought of this ribbon as you,
and had it on me every day.

1709
00:18:40,680 --> 00:18:42,040
Your Highness...

1710
00:18:44,330 --> 00:18:51,070
I have yet to attain it, but I'm positive
I will become a suitable fiancÃ©e for you.

1711
00:18:51,580 --> 00:18:54,530
As a member of the royal family, I will not bring shameâ€”

1712
00:18:54,530 --> 00:18:56,570
I'm sorry, Eli.

1713
00:18:56,970 --> 00:18:58,780
That's enough.

1714
00:18:58,780 --> 00:19:05,460
My Lady. Prince Christopher
has just returned from a long journey, and he is tired.

1715
00:19:05,710 --> 00:19:08,460
We must let him go now.

1716
00:19:09,530 --> 00:19:12,130
Are we under the tanuki's watchful eye?

1717
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:20,640
<i>The next day was the last of the hunting festival.</i>

1718
00:19:21,650 --> 00:19:27,150
<i>Count Hayden showed his remarkable skill,
as previously observed.</i>

1719
00:19:28,850 --> 00:19:35,150
<i>This year, the flower crown was dedicated
to the Princess Ladybird Sylvia. </i><i></i>

1720
00:19:37,390 --> 00:19:43,740
<i>Then, Lady Anna was able to confront
Count Hayden as she was determined to do. Â </i>

1721
00:19:44,930 --> 00:19:51,170
Father, right now I want to continue learning about history
more than I want to marry.

1722
00:19:51,610 --> 00:19:58,940
There is more than one way to live for a woman.
Lady Sylvia and Lady Elianna taught me that.

1723
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:02,820
Lady Elianna.

1724
00:20:04,060 --> 00:20:05,730
Lady Kreis.

1725
00:20:06,010 --> 00:20:10,770
Thanks to you, I was able to understand my friend's heart.

1726
00:20:10,770 --> 00:20:14,480
If her heart has been passed down to you, Lady Elianna,

1727
00:20:14,870 --> 00:20:17,990
then she still lives on in this land.

1728
00:20:25,520 --> 00:20:27,500
Lord Irvin, here.

1729
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:35,300
There's no point in a man having a book on embroidery.

1730
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:39,930
Then is it all right if I keep it?

1731
00:20:40,530 --> 00:20:42,760
Bibliophile Princess, huh...

1732
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:49,440
That's far more suitable for you
than such an extravagant name as the "Brain of Sauslind."

1733
00:20:50,260 --> 00:20:56,070
A country where people are not persecuted
just for liking their neighbors.

1734
00:20:56,070 --> 00:20:59,820
I'd like to see that someday as well, Lady Elianna.

1735
00:21:00,530 --> 00:21:03,150
The flowers of Eidel will bloom in the spring.

1736
00:21:03,150 --> 00:21:05,330
Please come and see them.

1737
00:21:07,220 --> 00:21:10,710
Will you belong to another man when spring comes?

1738
00:21:13,500 --> 00:21:17,960
What would happen if I snatched you up like my father did?

1739
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:23,600
Should I take that as a challenge?

1740
00:21:25,020 --> 00:21:26,580
I'm joking.

1741
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:34,110
Lady Elianna. I'm glad we met, Bibliophile Princess.

1742
00:21:40,180 --> 00:21:41,890
Let's go, Eli.

1743
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:45,340
Lord Chris.

1744
00:21:46,710 --> 00:21:48,250
What did you just say?

1745
00:21:49,340 --> 00:21:51,080
Lord Chris.

1746
00:21:51,080 --> 00:21:55,520
This is the first time you've called me that in front of others.

1747
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:58,510
This is late but...

1748
00:22:00,500 --> 00:22:04,220
Well, welcome back!

1749
00:22:05,600 --> 00:22:07,060
I'm home...

1750
00:22:07,060 --> 00:22:08,970
my ladybird.

